	'r1' => 'Measure the doorway and lay the mat, about 20 minutes.',
	'r2' => 'The mat stays in place; you do nothing to it.',
	'r3' => 'Still in place. If a wet spell packs the pile early, you can add a swap visit.',
	'r4' => 'Swap. The fitter rolls the used mat into the van and unrolls a fresh one on the same sill.',
	'round_depot' => 'Between visits the used mats are washed and inspected at the Canal Yard depot.',
	'round_h' => 'How the round works',
	'round_p' => 'Every mat on the round is swapped every four weeks. The fitter’s week is the same shape wherever the doorway is.',
	's1_h' => 'Offices',
	's1_p' => 'An office lobby takes a mat inside glass or revolving doors, where shoe grit meets a polished floor before the desks.',
	's2_h' => 'Shops',
	's2_p' => 'A shop doorway takes a slate mat just inside the glass, laid before the first customer and swapped on the same week-4 visit.',
	's3_h' => 'Clinics',
	's3_p' => 'A clinic reception stays calm and dry: the mat sits at the entrance, and the fitter is gone in about 20 minutes.',
	's4_h' => 'Showrooms',
	's4_p' => 'A showroom uses a wider mat on a polished floor so the threshold stays clean between client visits.',
	'search_results' => 'Search results for: %s',
